#
# Packages allowed to have a build script (`custom-build` target), checked by `cargo xtask
# check-build-scripts` over the whole dependency graph (ADR-0023 decision 1, NFR-SEC-10). One `name@version`
# per line, the version exactly as cargo reports it (build metadata included); a comment may follow, and it
# does not repeat the version. A new version of a listed crate fails the check until its build.rs is read again
# and `cargo xtask check-build-scripts --bless` re-versions the line (same comment, same place); bless never
# adds a crate. Add a crate only after reading its build.rs: no network access, no binary download, writes
# only under OUT_DIR. Downloader build scripts are banned (C-5).
#
# Reviewed at M0 (WP-S0.01): all of these run `rustc --version` or a probe compile to set cfg flags, and at
# most write a generated module to OUT_DIR.
#
# Added at M0 (WP-S0.02, xtask dependencies sha2 0.10 and spdx): generic-array 0.14.7 runs `rustc --version`
# through version_check and sets one cfg; libc 0.2.191 (via cpufeatures) runs `rustc --version`, and only on
# FreeBSD or Emscripten targets `freebsd-version` or `emcc --version`, then sets cfg flags. Neither writes files
# or uses the network.
anyhow@1.0.104
camino@1.2.6
generic-array@0.14.7
proc-macro2@1.0.107
quote@1.0.47
serde@1.0.229
serde_core@1.0.229
serde_json@1.0.154
thiserror@1.0.69 # re-read at cycle 20 (first version-keyed review): probe-compiles build/probe.rs into OUT_DIR/probe for one cfg flag; no network, no file outside OUT_DIR
thiserror@2.0.21
zmij@1.0.23
#
