libc@0.2.191 # runs `rustc --version` (and `freebsd-version` / `emcc -dumpversion` on those targets); cfg flags only
num-traits@0.2.19 # autocfg probe compile for one cfg flag (proptest, dev-only)
rustversion@1.0.23 # runs `rustc --version`, writes version.expr to OUT_DIR
wasm-bindgen@0.2.129 # wasm targets only in practice: version cfg via a vendored rustversion, link args for emscripten
wasm-bindgen-shared@0.2.129 # hashes two of its own source files into an env var; runs `git rev-parse HEAD` (local)
#
# Reviewed at WP-S3.01 (ew-dl and its dev-dependencies). Neither opens a network connection or downloads
# anything.
libm@0.2.16 # reads CARGO_* and TARGET env vars, emits cfg flags and rustc-env values only; writes no files
rustix@0.38.44 # re-read at cycle 20 (first version-keyed review; in the UI graph): probe-compiles snippets with rustc into OUT_DIR, deletes the artifact, emits cfg flags
rustix@1.1.5 # (tempfile via insta, dev-only) probe-compiles snippets with rustc into OUT_DIR, deletes the artifact, emits cfg flags
ref-cast@1.0.27 # (schemars, WP-S1.02) runs `rustc --version` for cfg flags, writes private.rs to OUT_DIR only
#
# Reviewed at WP-S3.02 (ew-text: parley's ICU4X line segmentation and normalisation data). The four build
# scripts are identical: they read the ICU4X_DATA_DIR environment variable and emit cfg flags only; they run no
# command, write no file and open no network connection.
icu_locale_fallback_data@2.3.0
icu_normalizer_data@2.3.0
icu_properties_data@2.3.0
icu_segmenter_data@2.3.0
#
# Reviewed at WP-S3.04 (vello_cpu, krilla). The only new build script runs `rustc --version` and emits cfg flags;
# it writes no file and opens no network connection.
crc32fast@1.5.2 # reads RUSTC, runs `$RUSTC --version`, emits rustc-check-cfg / rustc-cfg lines only
#
# Reviewed at WP-S1.10 (ew-sqlview: rusqlite 0.40.2 with `bundled`). The build script compiles the vendored
# sqlite3.c with cc into OUT_DIR and copies the pre-generated bindings (no bindgen without `buildtime_bindgen`);
# it reads only CARGO_*/TARGET/HOST and the documented SQLITE_MAX_*/LIBSQLITE3_FLAGS variables, runs no command
# but the C compiler cc invokes, downloads nothing and opens no network connection.
libsqlite3-sys@0.38.2 # cc-compiles the bundled SQLite amalgamation into OUT_DIR, emits link and cfg lines
#
# Reviewed at WP-S2.01 part 1 (egui 0.37, eframe on wgpu, rfd 0.17.2 and their transitive crates). No build script
# opens a network connection, downloads anything or writes outside OUT_DIR. Several are for targets the
# application does not build on a given OS (Android, wasm, the other Windows architectures).
# cfg flags only (cfg_aliases, version or target probes, sanitizer detection; no file written, no command but
# `rustc --version` where noted):
